      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "CIVIC SQUARE (5) has been thereabouts in his two starts to date and has attracted market support. Has been kept fresh with a month between runs after sticking on gamely into sixth first-up at Geelong, but has kept up to the mark with a Geelong jumpout win. Bold showing anticipated. TEEN TORQUE (10) brings the race-fit profile and has improved through the campaign, placing at Kyneton last start after a fourth on Pakenham Syntho. Suspect Nolen to push forward from the wide draw and take up the running. WOLLEMI (7) looks the pick from the pair of debutants with some neat recent jumpouts under his belt. Is drawn cosy for Gaudrey and hails from a sharp juvenile stable. Not taking lightly. ACTION POINT (1) was left with too much to do on debut when turning a long way off them and never really looked likely. Better for that and can make his presence felt this time.",
